MID_EV14_044_m01: <EDH>
MID_EV14_044_m01_001: Kill them... Destroy them. Turn them to ash!
MID_EV14_044_m01_002: It's that voice again...
MID_EV14_044_m01_003: Crush them, slay them! Offer me your soul!
MID_EV14_044_m01_004: Nghhh... Nghaaah!
MID_EV14_044_m01_005: I've had it up to here with you... Why don't you\nshut up already?
MID_EV14_044_m01_006: Destroy, kill, crush, slaughter...
MID_EV14_044_m01_007: Enough of your chatter in my head!
MID_EV14_044_m01_008: Get out. Whoever you think you are. Get out!
MID_EV14_044_m01_009: Haaah... Haaah... Haaah...
MID_EV14_044_m01_010: I wasn't even playing Obsidian...and I heard it.
MID_EV14_044_m01_011: That's never happened before. Is it because of\nwhat I did?
MID_EV14_044_m01_012: Hearing voices is supposed to be a sign of death for\none using Drake's treasures.
MID_EV14_044_m01_013: Am I out of time already?
MID_EV14_044_m01_014: No—not yet. Not while he's still alive.
MID_EV14_044_m01_015: I'm going to kill Bertrand, whatever I have to\nsacrifice along the way!
MID_EV14_045_m01: <EDH>
MID_EV14_045_m01_001: Once again, it's time for your routine administrative\nannouncement for the Heroic Games.
MID_EV14_045_m01_002: Congratulations to the members of Rose Tempest!
MID_EV14_045_m01_003: With eight clans having emerged from the qualifiers,\nthe stage is set!
MID_EV14_045_m01_004: The main matches are about to begin.
MID_EV14_045_m01_005: How do you all feel heading into the next phase?\nEnthusiastic?
MID_EV14_045_m01_006: Fearless. We shall be the ones to come out\nvictorious! No one else!
MID_EV14_045_m01_007: And the splendor of a Rose of Caelus shall be burned\ninto the memories of all who watch!
MID_EV14_045_m01_008: No matter what she's going through, Olympia's\nalways...well, Olympia.
MID_EV14_045_m01_009: Good to see you're fired up! I am too. It'll be a treat\nto watch you all out there.
MID_EV14_045_m01_010: Anyway, the bracket for the main matches is all\ndrawn up. Take a look!
MID_EV14_045_m01_012: Oh, I think I recognize...all of these names. We're in\nfor some stiff competition.
MID_EV14_045_m01_013: Of course! This lineup has all our strongest players.\nIt's bound to be a dazzling spectacle!
MID_EV14_045_m01_014: Hang on—that's not a clan I've heard of. Can you\ntell us about them?
MID_EV14_045_m01_015: The Fiery Mane! Good eye—you're right, they\nweren't in the qualifiers.
MID_EV14_045_m01_016: That's the clan of the famed White-Maned Demon!\nGot added to the roster after an exhibition match.
MID_EV14_045_m01_017: I guess Lord Solel wanted to add a little bit more\nexcitement to the games.
MID_EV14_045_m01_018: Bertrand's going to be in the main matches?!
MID_EV14_045_m01_019: I'll finally be able to take him on...and avenge\nmy father...
MID_EV14_045_m01_020: Going by the bracket, it seems like Bertrand\nwould be...the final opponent we face.
MID_EV14_045_m01_021: Assuming he makes it that far. And we do.
MID_EV14_045_m01_022: The finals... So far away. If only I could face\nhim sooner.
MID_EV14_045_m01_023: One can't always account for bad luck, Leilidahna.
MID_EV14_045_m01_024: Well! I've got places to be. Take care, and make sure\nyou prepare for your next match!
MID_EV14_045_m01_025: Hrmm...
MID_EV14_045_m01_026: Mu. I'd like to ask you a favor.
MID_EV14_045_m01_027: Only I can't talk about it here. Find me later.
MID_EV14_045_m01_028: Ah, ye— Sure thing, Leda.
MID_EV14_045_m01_029: Aww...
MID_EV14_045_m01_030: You're looking sullen, Mu. What was the favor\nMiss Leda asked? Something distressing?
MID_EV14_045_m01_031: Yeah. She asked me to go to Credna's temple and\ndeliver this letter to Orchel.
MID_EV14_045_m01_032: Can I see it? So, she... Hmm.
MID_EV14_045_m01_033: She intends to discuss something with Miss Orchel\nin private.
MID_EV14_045_m01_034: When Miss Leda saw the bracket, she did complain\nthat the match against Bertrand was so far away.
MID_EV14_045_m01_035: If he were, hypothetically, eliminated in an earlier\nmatch, she could not see her revenge through.
MID_EV14_045_m01_036: You suggest she's...what? Blackmailing Bertrand's\nopponents into throwing their matches? Please!
MID_EV14_045_m01_037: I... I think milady's capable of it.
MID_EV14_045_m01_038: Either way, it's not very sporting behavior.
MID_EV14_045_m01_039: I don't understand. What is her hurry?
MID_EV14_045_m01_040: Milady...
MID_EV14_046_m01: <EDH>
MID_EV14_046_m01_001: Evening, kitten. Your look's changed since\nthe qualifier.
MID_EV14_046_m01_002: It has, hasn't it? But it's still me, through and\nthrough. Hello, Leda.
MID_EV14_046_m01_003: So you're the one who sent the letter. What's\nthis all about?
MID_EV14_046_m01_004: I'll try to make it quick.
MID_EV14_046_m01_005: I heard your first main match in the games is against\nthe White-Maned Demon.
MID_EV14_046_m01_006: Yes... I just found that out.
MID_EV14_046_m01_007: Right. Would you lose against him? Or withdraw\nin advance?
MID_EV14_046_m01_008: Ah... Could I ask why?
MID_EV14_046_m01_009: I need him to make it to the finals. To face me.
MID_EV14_046_m01_010: The White-Maned Demon murdered my father,\nand I have to get my revenge.
MID_EV14_046_m01_011: We all...carry burdens. Life demands different things\nfrom each of us.
MID_EV14_046_m01_012: Leda, arrange a meeting with the White-Maned\nDemon. Discuss all of this.
MID_EV14_046_m01_013: There may be more to this than you know. I'm not\nsaying put aside revenge. Just...talk first.
MID_EV14_046_m01_014: Don't! You don't know me or what I've been through.\nAnd it's none of your business anyway!
MID_EV14_046_m01_015: He cannot be taken by anyone else. Killing him is all\nI have to live for!
MID_EV14_046_m01_016: Leda... Turn back from this. Your soul is in the\ngrip of something terrifying.
MID_EV14_046_m01_017: It's very serious—far beyond anything that people\nshould ever experience.
MID_EV14_046_m01_018: Hmm. So, you're not even going to consider helping.\nIs that it?
MID_EV14_046_m01_019: Yes, I suppose. I do have my own reasons to be in\nthe games, after all.
MID_EV14_046_m01_020: In that case... You know, I'd hate if the cat priest had\nan accident here.
MID_EV14_046_m01_021: But if she did, well, I suppose Bertrand would win by\ndefault and advance in the games.
MID_EV14_046_m01_022: Leda, don't you realize—your fury is getting the\nbest of you! You're just redirecting it to me!
MID_EV14_046_m01_023: Besides, I won't give up what I want. Not to\nsomeone here for the wrong reasons.
MID_EV14_046_m01_024: Yeah, how noble of you. You should have agreed to\nmy request. Since you didn't...
MID_EV14_046_m01_025: Stop, Leda! You mustn't—not here, not ever!
MID_EV14_046_m01_026: Ngh...
MID_EV14_046_m01_027: Obsidian's power is... What the hell? What ARE you?
MID_EV14_046_m01_028: I'm less and less sure of that myself...
MID_EV14_046_m01_029: I can say that a real darkness surrounds that\nvihuela of yours.
MID_EV14_046_m01_030: So, please... Don't use it much—or at all.
MID_EV14_046_m01_031: Shut up! You think I'll stop fighting?
MID_EV14_046_m01_032: May the Demon snap your neck!
MID_EV14_046_m01_033: No, wait! You must look after your soul!
MID_EV14_108_m01: <EDH>
MID_EV14_108_m01_001: *sigh*
MID_EV14_108_m01_002: Sirocco. Why are you out so late?
MID_EV14_108_m01_003: I surge like the winds across Lake Baal, upon which\nthis city stands!
MID_EV14_108_m01_004: You know exactly why a man like me would be out\nin the middle of the night.
MID_EV14_108_m01_005: Uh-huh. Sorry, I just can't help but notice how\nnervous you are.
MID_EV14_108_m01_006: I find it hard to believe you're off to visit a woman.
MID_EV14_108_m01_007: Interesting. What makes you think I'm nervous?
MID_EV14_108_m01_008: Your footsteps. When you're nervous, there's a slight\nscraping sound—your toes drag.
MID_EV14_108_m01_009: I'd guess that it's an unconscious habit. You do it\nwhen you're in Kalla's presence as well.
MID_EV14_108_m01_010: I knew you had a good ear, but... Color me\nimpressed.
MID_EV14_108_m01_011: You're clearly not scampering off to one of your\nlate-night trysts.
MID_EV14_108_m01_012: So, where are you going? Come on. Out with it.
MID_EV14_108_m01_013: Gods, you're sharp. Fine. I'll tell you.
MID_EV14_108_m01_014: The guesthouse where the Aragonians are staying—\nI want to go there and dig into something.
MID_EV14_108_m01_015: Didn't you admonish me for wanting to do the\nsame thing?
MID_EV14_108_m01_016: Well, one of us keeps trying to kill people, and it's\nnot me.
MID_EV14_108_m01_017: I just wanted to take a quick look. Some furtive\ninvestigation, and I leave.
MID_EV14_108_m01_018: I'm the wind. I can slip through with ease.
MID_EV14_108_m01_019: Then we'll go together. Now we know the kingdom's\nour enemy, after all.
MID_EV14_108_m01_020: Best that we learn as much as we can about them.
MID_EV14_109_m01: <EDH>
MID_EV14_109_m01_001: We have to get rid of him. We have to!
MID_EV14_109_m01_002: What is the Divine Sovereign thinking, letting that\nman enter the games?
MID_EV14_109_m01_003: Bertrand survives, while Aswan and I drift apart.
MID_EV14_109_m01_004: Nothing ever goes my way!
MID_EV14_109_m01_005: Gilchris, dear, be calm. All will be well.
MID_EV14_109_m01_006: You know I'll take care of you, don't you?
MID_EV14_109_m01_007: Stepmother, you're the only person I trust in\nthis world. You can't leave me.
MID_EV14_109_m01_008: That woman is...beautiful. Who is she?
MID_EV14_109_m01_009: Well, the man she's talking to, I believe that's\nKing Gilchris.
MID_EV14_109_m01_010: Which would mean she is none other than\nChancellor Martila of Arago.
MID_EV14_109_m01_011: She has been described by many as the most\nbeautiful woman in the world.
MID_EV14_109_m01_012: Which might be an understatement. What a\nspectacular sight! Ah, but...
MID_EV14_109_m01_013: *sniff* As I thought.
MID_EV14_109_m01_014: Uh, Sirocco? What are you doing?
MID_EV14_109_m01_015: Miss Leda, that's the woman we saw at\nthe lakehouse.
MID_EV14_109_m01_016: How can you be sure?
MID_EV14_109_m01_017: I smell it. The chancellor is using a fragrance derived\nof ambergris from the southern sea...
MID_EV14_109_m01_018: the same as that woman.
MID_EV14_109_m01_019: I know ambergris isn't cheap, but it is fairly common\namong those who can afford it.
MID_EV14_109_m01_020: Even Kalla uses that. What you're describing is\na coincidence.
MID_EV14_109_m01_021: No, the notes of a perfume are altered or amplified\nby the woman who wears it.
MID_EV14_109_m01_022: The same fragrance, combined with different sweats\nand body odors, can produce infinite scent profiles.
MID_EV14_109_m01_023: Coming from you, this is sounding...uncomfortably\nanatomical.
MID_EV14_109_m01_024: Her aroma—like that of a breezy spring day—mixing\nwith the sweet ambergris...
MID_EV14_109_m01_025: I'm sure. That woman we saw and the chancellor,\nthey're the same person.
MID_EV14_109_m01_026: Oh, and...likely Maria as well.
MID_EV14_109_m01_027: What?!
MID_EV14_109_m01_028: Damn it— Miss Leda, lower your voice!
MID_EV14_109_m01_029: Who goes there?
MID_EV14_109_m01_030: I heard it too. Guards, after the intruder!
MID_EV14_109_m01_031: Nothing for it—time to go. Like the wind!
MID_EV14_109_m01_032: That was close. I'm surprised we managed to get\nout of there, but... *sigh*
MID_EV14_109_m01_033: It hardly seems like that was your first time\nslinking around.
MID_EV14_109_m01_034: Well...there are many things a vulkan is asked to do.
MID_EV14_109_m01_035: And for my lady, I'll gladly hide anywhere. A burrow\nor the bottom of the sea.
MID_EV14_047_m01: <EDH>
MID_EV14_047_m01_001: Aaand the main matches have begun! Ready to\nwin it, Leda?
MID_EV14_047_m01_002: Ready for it to be over.
MID_EV14_047_m01_003: I have to reach that man as soon as I can...
MID_EV14_047_m01_004: Uh... Leda?
MID_EV14_047_m01_005: Cai is no ordinary boy.
MID_EV14_047_m01_006: There are signs that he's being backed by the temple\nof Aurora.
MID_EV14_047_m01_007: But I suppose to make Buccar happy, it would be\nbetter if we lost.
MID_EV14_047_m01_008: What are you talking about?
MID_EV14_047_m01_009: We're all on the same side, Sirocco. Buccar wants to\nwin like the rest of us!
MID_EV14_047_m01_010: Ehh... Hm.
MID_EV14_047_m01_011: Syracusio, you go too far. MUCH too far!
MID_EV14_047_m01_012: You have somehow managed to exceed your own\nimpressive record for rudeness!
MID_EV14_047_m01_013: Why is everyone... What's going on? You're all\nso tense.
MID_EV14_047_m01_014: *sigh*
MID_EV14_047_m01_015: Did I do something to upset you? Is that it?
MID_EV14_047_m01_016: I'm going to get some air.
MID_EV14_047_m01_017: Ugh...
MID_EV14_047_m01_018: It's getting really hard to tell what she's thinking.
MID_EV14_047_m01_019: I still love her, but... *sigh*
MID_EV14_047_m01_020: It feels like there's a part of Leda we're losing.\nLike she's going somewhere far away.
MID_EV14_047_m01_021: Mu, do you know the legend of Bloodaxe Hanno?
MID_EV14_047_m01_022: He was the king of Arago and wielded a fearsome\nweapon called the Bloodaxe.
MID_EV14_047_m01_023: The man began his reign beloved. Expanded Arago's\nterritory, became a champion to his people.
MID_EV14_047_m01_024: But then—in his later years, fraught by delusion—\nhe turned into their tormentor.
MID_EV14_047_m01_025: After 13 years on the throne, he was assassinated.
MID_EV14_047_m01_026: So... Wait. Was the Bloodaxe one of Drake's\ntreasures? Like Obsidian?
MID_EV14_047_m01_027: It was. And the treasures always corrupt their users'\nsouls in time.
MID_EV14_047_m01_028: I wonder if Miss Leda is getting impatient because\nshe can feel the corruption growing.
MID_EV14_047_m01_029: You think it's eaten that much of her soul already?
MID_EV14_047_m01_030: I didn't say that. Miss Leda is strong. And I'll see her\nstory to its end—whatever that might be.
MID_EV14_047_m01_031: Syracusio, are you not overestimating her ability\nto survive this?
MID_EV14_047_m01_032: Leilidahna is merely human. An ordinary\nyoung woman!
MID_EV14_047_m01_033: Hmm...
MID_EV14_047_m01_034: Surely you won't stand by and watch her saunter off\nto her doom.
MID_EV14_047_m01_035: If we cannot come to Leilidahna's aid, then what\nare we?
MID_EV14_047_m01_036: Could we even call ourselves her friends?
MID_EV14_047_m01_037: Buccar, help us out here! What do we do?
MID_EV14_047_m01_038: I don't want anything to happen to Leda!
MID_EV14_047_m01_039: Rrgh...
MID_EV14_048_m01: <EDH>
MID_EV14_048_m01_001: I've been looking for you, Leda. I want to talk to you\nabout something.
MID_EV14_048_m01_002: Back on your feet already? You should be resting,\nshouldn't you?
MID_EV14_048_m01_003: Oh. It's...nice to know you're such a thoughtful\nperson, Leda.
MID_EV14_048_m01_004: Because you fought like a demon in the games.
MID_EV14_048_m01_005: But you seem kind, like I thought you'd be, even\nthough I didn't have any reason for thinking that.
MID_EV14_048_m01_006: <NCA>Show exasperation.
MID_EV14_048_m01_007: <NCB>Give him praise.
MID_EV14_048_m01_008: <ACA>I was fully prepared to end your life!
MID_EV14_048_m01_009: <ACA>I know you're new to this, but... You don't try making\nnice with the person who almost killed you.
MID_EV14_048_m01_010: <ACB>You did well out there. In a few years, I wager you'll\nbe unbeatable, just about.
MID_EV14_048_m01_011: <ACB>You really think so? That's quite a compliment\ncoming from a fighter like you.
MID_EV14_048_m01_012: I guess you're feeling better than you were during\nour match.
MID_EV14_048_m01_013: Wh-what is THAT supposed to mean?!
MID_EV14_048_m01_014: Leda, if you're matched against Bertrand, will \nyou really, you know...
MID_EV14_048_m01_015: Of course I will. I'm killing him the moment I\nsee him...even if it kills me too.
MID_EV14_048_m01_016: I like Bertrand. I don't want either of you to die.
MID_EV14_048_m01_017: Leda, do you really need vengeance that badly?\nCan't you stop this?
MID_EV14_048_m01_018: No— No. It doesn't work that way. This is all that's\nkept me going.
MID_EV14_048_m01_019: To hate someone passionately...it's not unlike being\nin love.
MID_EV14_048_m01_020: I don't really know that much about being in love.
MID_EV14_048_m01_021: Oh? Well, I'm sure you'll find out soon enough.
MID_EV14_048_m01_022: Whether you're asleep or awake, a single person\noccupies your every thought.
MID_EV14_048_m01_023: You hate them, but it doesn't end there. This person\ncontrols your actions, your heart...your everything.
MID_EV14_048_m01_024: This feeling drives you—drives everything about\nyou—and soon nothing else has meaning.
MID_EV14_048_m01_025: Eventually, you feel like you have to go along with it,\nbecause if you don't, you'll lose yourself entirely.
MID_EV14_048_m01_026: But, Leda, there are people who love you and care\nabout you.
MID_EV14_048_m01_027: I think Buccar was really worried when he saw what\nyou'd become.
MID_EV14_048_m01_028: Hm...
MID_EV14_048_m01_029: You should forgive Buccar, at least.
MID_EV14_048_m01_030: He just cares about you, Leda, probably more than\nanyone else.
MID_EV14_048_m01_031: You think I don't know that? I have...a lot to say to\nhim, though.
MID_EV14_048_m01_032: Then say it. Clear the air, and start over.
MID_EV14_048_m01_033: Mmm. I'll think about it.
MID_EV14_049_m01: <EDH>
MID_EV14_049_m01_001: Anna? Ah! The results of your investigation, please.
MID_EV14_049_m01_002: We scoured the hiding spot Leda mentioned.
MID_EV14_049_m01_003: And recovered a large supply of orichalcum, which\nshe said had been extracted from the ghost carriage.
MID_EV14_049_m01_004: Seems she was telling the truth.
MID_EV14_049_m01_005: We can hardly ignore the smuggling of orichalcum to\nthe temple.
MID_EV14_049_m01_006: Nor Leda's claim—which this proves—that it's being\nmined in Cydonia.
MID_EV14_049_m01_007: Lord Solel, can I ask? Why did you allow the\nkingdom of Arago to take over Cydonia?
MID_EV14_049_m01_008: Proximity was a factor. The county is closer to Grand\nAragon, Arago's capital, than to Dagsion.
MID_EV14_049_m01_009: That land was always intended to be incorporated\ninto Arago, and governed thereby.
MID_EV14_049_m01_010: We whom they call "gods" may live longer than\nhumans, but we are not immortal.
MID_EV14_049_m01_011: The progenitor god bade us guide humankind...\nbut someday, we will be gone.
MID_EV14_049_m01_012: So, we've long meant to hand governance of the\nlands over to the humans.
MID_EV14_049_m01_013: When the chancellor of Arago proposed to take\ncontrol of Cydonia, I saw an opportunity.
MID_EV14_049_m01_014: A chance to set an example for a new era of human\nstewardship. But perhaps I acted too rashly.
MID_EV14_049_m01_015: That reminds me—it seems Chancellor Martila is\ntied to the Order of Mithras. As suspected.
MID_EV14_049_m01_016: It could be the earlier shipments of orichalcum are\nin their hands.
MID_EV14_049_m01_017: I can't believe how badly I've underestimated the\nOrder's influence.
MID_EV14_049_m01_018: You don't think— Is it possible they knew orichalcum\ncould be mined in Cydonia?
MID_EV14_049_m01_019: And orchestrated events so the county would be\nadded to Arago?
MID_EV14_049_m01_020: The basis for my decision was testimony by Mahdel,\nhigh priest at the time.
MID_EV14_049_m01_021: Despite him having been discharged from service due\nto scandal, I did trust him.
MID_EV14_049_m01_022: The scandal, I'd heard, was concocted to protect a\nyoung human.
MID_EV14_049_m01_023: So I took his testimony against the viceroy as\nplain truth.
MID_EV14_049_m01_024: But if he was under the Order's sway...
MID_EV14_049_m01_025: Anna, continue your investigation, bearing in mind\nthat we don't know how far their tendrils reach.
MID_EV14_049_m01_026: Take care that our movements aren't known to the\nOrder of Mithras.
MID_EV14_049_m01_027: You're not saying what I think you are.
MID_EV14_049_m01_028: That we're parting ways with them? Yes. Even if it\nmeans war.
MID_EV14_049_m01_029: How many troops can we mobilize before Magistra\nRaksha finds out?
MID_EV14_049_m01_030: I've been investigating this in secret since you asked\nme to. I still am.
MID_EV14_049_m01_031: But it's tricky. I don't know how deep into the\ntemples they're sunk in.
MID_EV14_049_m01_032: Give me three months. I can probably scrounge up\nsome kind of fighting force.
MID_EV14_049_m01_033: Do it. Time is not on our side.
MID_EV14_049_m01_034: Lord Solel... A question. One I've had for a while.
MID_EV14_049_m01_035: The Order was founded by Dagda the Great to\nhonor Magistra Raksha.
MID_EV14_049_m01_036: When you became Divine Sovereign, you could've\ndissolved it—but you didn't.
MID_EV14_049_m01_037: Why not? Why did you trust them?
MID_EV14_049_m01_038: I owed them a debt. My wife, Yu Phas, she... *sigh*
MID_EV14_049_m01_039: But in the time since, the balance has fallen too\nsteeply to their side.
MID_EV14_049_m01_040: Now I know I must even it out. That is my\nresponsibility.